  "details": "I just realized that when using most avatars that are uploaded for crossplatform, the PC version has better ranking like... let's say that was ranked as medium, for example. However on when comes to the Quest/Android version, turns out that has a ranking of \"Very poor\", which annoys me when I decide which to wear for quest users and will show the fallback instead for them. In the end, those that are marked as crossplatform aren't that at all and feels more like a PC only avatar. I am aware that \"Very poor\" avatars will be removed on Quest in the future.\n\nI thought that can be done by adding a performance rank indicator icon for the Quest/Android version on the PC platform and viceversa. The concept image attached to this post will visually show what I mean by that. The colored performance rank icon indicates which platform you are currently on, similar to the PC/Mobile Diagram that shows which platform is the content posted on. For the greyed out icons, you can tell which one is the performance rank by its shape within the circle. Only applies to crossplatform avatars, any platform exclusives (PC only or Mobile only content) will remain unchanged.",
